CLOUD SECRETS (DO NOT COMMIT THE REAL VALUES)

REQUIRED FOR YOUTUBE PUBLISHING
YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET_B64
  Base64 of credentials/client_secret.json
YOUTUBE_TOKEN_B64
  Base64 of credentials/token.json after the one-time OAuth authorization.

OPTIONAL, BUT NEEDED FOR TREND DISCOVERY
YOUTUBE_API_KEY
  Raw YouTube Data API v3 key (not base64).

OPTIONAL FOR ONE ORIGINAL TREND-INSPIRED AI IMAGE PER DAY
OPENAI_API_KEY
  OpenAI Images API key (raw, not base64); API billing is separate from a ChatGPT subscription. If absent, AI image generation is skipped.

OPTIONAL FOR FACEBOOK PUBLISHING
FACEBOOK_PAGE_B64
  Base64 of credentials/facebook_page.json. JSON fields:
  page_id, page_access_token, graph_api_version (for example v24.0).

OPTIONAL FOR INSTAGRAM TREND DISCOVERY
INSTAGRAM_ACCESS_TOKEN_B64
  Base64 of a text file containing the Instagram access token.
INSTAGRAM_USER_ID
  Raw Instagram professional-account user ID.
INSTAGRAM_GRAPH_API_VERSION
  Graph API version such as v24.0.

Termux examples:
  base64 -w 0 credentials/client_secret.json
  base64 -w 0 credentials/token.json
  base64 -w 0 credentials/facebook_page.json
  printf '%s' 'YOUR_INSTAGRAM_TOKEN' | base64 -w 0

For GitHub: Repository -> Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> New repository secret.
Set each secret directly in GitHub. Never paste token/key values into ChatGPT, source files, or public issues.
